body:
GREG, 2026-11-06 about 16:27Z, relayed by Engram::Asistant (mailbox 43498a6e #402, message e99bac4b), verbatim: „NIE ... PO TO MAMY SOURCE_ID ktory rozwiazuje te problemy wszyscy maja uzywac tylko source_id”.
Asistant's reading: every consumer judging source identity or state uses ONE shared source_id. No parallel fingerprints, no watcher-event dependencies, no .git hashing. This covers option B AND the launcher, gates and the general EO model.
At the time: the Windows Central PAUSE (Asistant #396, 16:25Z) was in force; inventory only, no implementation.
Engram's inventory sent to Greg (Asistant #403, 16:28Z):
(1) the launcher's own input fingerprint (scripts/review-freeze-fingerprint.mjs, test-launcher.mjs; docs/development.md ~800–831) with new-untracked-only and the .git/info checks, which is also referenced in the AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md landing rule and test-ref names (w-0675 territory);
(2) Engram's general EO model accepting TermAl turn observations whose source_revision may be TermAl content-v1, plus watcher_only changes that stale checks;
(3) acceptance evaluation and `done --source-fingerprint` comparing source strings (evaluations OFF; existing ones untouched);
(4) review freeze by Git tree id for uncommitted input; proposal: commits only;
(5) scripts/eo-cutover.mjs fingerprint use, role unknown.
Proposed order: 1, then 2 with TermAl, then 3 at evaluation re-enable. Nothing changes without Greg's word. TermAl's inventory was requested from Fable2 (#6753).
